# Intent: the away-from-home fallback must work whatever Wi-Fi the friend has and must never hand the pairing token to a stranger's network (owner 2026-11-14: 'this needs to be robust to work whatever his home wifi is'). Patch 144 tried a fixed 192.168.2.1; macOS Internet Sharing may pick another subnet, so the fallback host is now the unit's current Wi-Fi default GATEWAY first (the laptop on its own Internet Sharing network, any subnet), then 192.168.2.1, chosen at each attempt. The fallback only runs on a network whose name starts with CONFIG_STACKCHAN_FALLBACK_SSID_PREFIX (default 'maipai', case-insensitive): the owner names the laptop's sharing network 'maipai-trip', the unit joins it only with its WPA2 password, so a friend's router or a hotel never receives the saved token, and a lookalike network cannot join without the password.
# Check after a flash: on a network named maipai-trip with the home address unreachable the serial log says 'fallback host for attempt N: <gateway>'; on any other network it says 'fallback not used: this Wi-Fi network is not a maipai* network' and no connection is attempted to its gateway; core test: body/tests/firmware/fallback_core_test.c.
